course: dictionary
lesson: 15972
title: The word unwitting
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Unwitting means you do not know something, or you are not aware of what you are doing. Look for clues in the words around it. «Mia carried the parcel to the door, not knowing it held stolen goods.» The words not knowing are the clue, so unwitting must mean not aware.
explain: «He made an unwitting mistake when he pressed the wrong button.» A mistake that is made without meaning to is an accident. The word unwitting tells you Tom did not mean to press the wrong button.
explain: Stories often use unwitting for a character who helps without knowing the truth. Ask yourself: did the character know what was happening? If not, unwitting is probably the right word. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Unwitting means not knowing or not aware of what is happening.
fact: «An unwitting mistake» is a mistake made by accident, without meaning to.
fact: «Unwittingly» is the adverb: «She unwittingly told the secret to her little brother.»
fact: In stories, an unwitting helper is a character who helps without realising a crime is happening.
exercise: «The unwitting helper carried the box for the thief.» What does unwitting mean here? | Happy to help the thief | *Not knowing what was in the box | Angry with the thief | Very strong and tall
exercise: «He made an unwitting mistake when he pressed the wrong button.» What kind of mistake was it? | Very large and loud | Made on purpose to annoy his teacher | Made twice on purpose | *Made by accident, without meaning to
exercise: Which phrase means most nearly the same as unwitting? | *Not aware | Wide awake | Full of anger | Very clever
test: «Sam was an unwitting accomplice; he drove the car without knowing about the robbery.» What does this tell you about Sam? | He knew everything about the plan | He planned the robbery himself | He was the police officer | *He did not realise what he was helping with
test: «She unwittingly told the secret to her brother.» What does unwittingly tell you about how she told it? | *She did not realise she was giving away a secret | Loudly, so everyone could hear | Angrily, to hurt him | Carefully, on purpose
exam: What is an unwitting victim? | *Someone who did not know they were being tricked or harmed | Someone who chose to be hurt | A very brave hero | A winner of a prize
